  "id": "social-incentive",
  "term": "social incentive",
  "definition": "A social incentive is a social factor that encourages people’s behavior, such as influence from others, features of their social network, and trust in other people or institutions. In this context, it refers to social conditions that can motivate attitude change and support desired actions.",
